he lake actually  puts forward a challenge to the  scenarios objective and I think it's  clear to see why this scenario is often  considered to be more fun now to nuance  this a bit and to show that I'm not just  cherry picking these examples rct2 does  do it right in some cases rainbow  valleys objectives for instance state  that you cannot build above three  Heights so the level design consists of  huge Hills that allow you to build large  terrain conforming coasters to fit with  this height restriction that said I  think this is a major reason why so many  people feel like RCT one scenarios are  more memorable and more fun but don't  really know why they feel that way some  things just right about the way the  scenarios play out because there's a  connection between what the game gives  you and what the game asks you to make  that's and the fact that you actually  have to play the scenarios to unlock  more which is a pretty good way to get  you motivated and also the research  department is actually necessary in RCT  one because you start out with only if  you rides most of the time unlike the  majority of ICT to scenarios where  you're given way too many rides right  from the start I do like our city to  though just as much as the other games I  just think that the scenarios dropped  the ball in some ways and maybe this is  why some people prefer the original over  the second one the critical reception  was also a little bit less good on the  second game but to be honest I don't  think this is really too relevant  looking back now because most of the  criticism was that the second game  didn't really add much to the first game  and it was more of an expansion pack  than a real new game but to be honest  the original game is just that good I  can't really blame them for not changing  anything about it and finally rct3  arguably continued down the same path  ICT 2 went and really just took it a  step further the game being in 3d and  including a sandbox mode only made it  more popular as a creative tool where  you can design and ride your own roller  coasters and even walk around in your  own theme parks the game added tons of  other content as well like firework  shows water parks and even animals so  you can build zoos in this game out of  any of these games this is probably the  one that I spend most time playing and I  never really got tired of the sandbox  mode because there's just so much  content and pretty much from 2010 to  2015 this is the game that I made videos  off on YouTube and this is the game  that's sort of the reason that I'm even  here and making this video right now  that said people never really seem to  play this game for the actual campaign  mode and even if I do think the career  mode is kind of underrated and  definitely really ambitious  it just doesn't live up to how its  height the management in the original  game is also the graphics didn't really  age well even if this game was  impressive when it came out I might go  back to this at some point in the future  if I get my disc back and maybe I'll  make some videos of some of the coasters  that I never finished in this game but  that said going back to this right now  really doesn't feel as intuitive  or friendly as going back to roller  coaster tycoon one or two there's just  something about the strange cartoony  very low poly style of 3d arts that the  game has part for what's next it's hard  to say what impact roller coaster tycoon  had on the simulation game genre twenty  years ago obviously it created a trilogy  that remains popular and well respected  to this day but the last entry in this  trilogy came up 15 years ago what else  did it bring since then okay  so just because I need to get this out  of the way there have been many attempts  by Atari who to this day owned the  rights to the franchise to milk it for  all it's worth and I don't think there  is anything I can say here that hasn't  been said many times already aside from  the ports these games are all explicitly  made to trick customers into buying them  because name recognition I guess while  keeping their development costs as low  as possible some of them are better than  others but they're all bad I'm gonna  list them all here just to get this over  with and so you know what not to spend  your money on  there's roller coaster tycoon 3d roller  coaster tycoon for mobile rollercoaster  tycoon world  roller coaster tycoon touch which is a  port of roller coaster tycoon world and  most recently roller coaster tycoon  adventures which is a ports of roller  coaster tycoon touch which was a port of  roller coaster tycoon world this time  it's for the switch and then there's  also roller coaster tycoon adventures  for PC which you can find on the Epic  Games Store which is not something that  we all have but that's what it's limited  to unfortunately and yeah this game is a  part of roller coaster tycoon adventures  for the switch which was a port of  roller coaster tycoon touch which was a  port of roller coaster tycoon world  I hope row up to speed there honestly I  think at the moment there are really  only two true spiritual successors to  RCT there is planet coaster developed by  frontier and led by some of the people  who worked on rct2 and  three and on the other hand there is  also pork attacks which is a standalone  indie game which takes a lot of  inspiration from the original ICT but it  doesn't quite have the same connection  to it I don't want to dedicate too much  of my time to these other games in a  video which should be a celebration of  rollercoaster tycoon but in my opinion  anyone who wants to get back into this  small genre of theme park sims should  look into either of these two games  they're both great for very different  reasons and maybe that's something I'll  get into later that said they're pretty  much the bulk of my channel so I'm not  too sure if I'm ready to make a  comparison video of these and honestly I  both love them equally for very  different reasons anyway that's it I  feel like there's a lot more I could say  about this game but I'm already  procrastinating on my homework by  writing this script now so I'll leave it  at this let me know what you loved about  the original roller coaster tycoon  though and I'll get back to making  videos on whichever new RCT inspired  game comes out
 

